<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PLAYER overflow menu. Two rows as of G3.

  Source: canonical `Menu / Плеер` 2444:18763 (206x264, r20, `menuSurface` on a
  1px `menuOutline`), widened to 260 by the frozen proposal
  `sleep-timer-menu-active` 2517:2093 whose note is explicit - "The canonical menu
  is 206 wide, which cannot hold a label plus a trailing value. Widened to 260.
  This is the only change proposed to the existing menu."

  ## Two rows of the frozen four

  The frozen menu has four, in this order: Найти трек, **Таймер сна**, **Сообщить
  о проблеме**, История эфира. The two in bold exist and are drawn; the other two
  do not exist and are absent rather than inert.

  That rule is not new here. An inert row is tolerable when it names a feature the
  app genuinely has and cannot reach yet - `Row / Аватар` on
  profile-authenticated - and is not tolerable when it names a feature with no
  implementation behind it at all, because it is then a dead control asserting
  that something exists. `SleepTimerSurfacesTest` has held it since G2 and still
  does; only the membership of its two lists moved.

  The two shipping rows keep their frozen **relative order**. Nothing is promoted
  to close the gap left by Найти трек: the menu is the frozen menu with two rows
  missing, not a new two-row menu.

  ## Geometry - the compact row, by owner override (G4a review)

  The frozen primitive (screens-3.6.6/spec/primitives.mjs:184) puts a 48 icon
  slot at x=12 in each row, the label at x=70, and 50 of padding under the last
  row. Rendered, that measured identical to the file within 0.76dp - and the
  owner rejected it on the rendered surface: the icon sat 38dp in from the card
  edge and the menu carried a 50dp empty band. This is an explicit override of
  the frozen frame, applied identically to this menu and to `Menu / Коллекция`:

      menu            260 wide, r20, 1px outline, no shadow   (unchanged)
      padding         10 top, 10 bottom                        (was 10 / 50)
      row             238x48 at x=11, pitch 52                 (unchanged)
      content         16 from the card edge on both sides      (row pad 5 + 11)
      icon            24x24 box at card-x 16                   (was a 48 slot at 23)
      label           card-x 56, 16 after the icon             (was 81)
      trailing        right-aligned, ending 16 from the card   (was 11)

  So two rows are 10 + 48 + 4 + 48 + 10 = **120** tall, not 160. The icon-16 /
  label-56 rhythm is not invented for this: it is the one every settings and
  profile row in the frozen file already uses, so the menus read as the same
  family as the lists they open over.

  The G2 / G3 history - a 10 / 10 single-row menu, then the frozen 50 restored
  as a debt G3 paid - is superseded rather than continued: one row and two rows
  now share the same 10 of bottom padding.

  ## The report row is absent in a build with no report endpoint

  See PlayerOverflowMenu. A build without `report.properties` draws the one-row
  menu - 10 + 48 + 10 = 68 - under the same compact padding as the two-row one.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/player_overflow_root"
    android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_width"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:background="@drawable/bg_player_overflow_menu"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:paddingTop="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_pad_top"
    android:paddingBottom="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_pad_bottom">

    <!-- `Menu row / Таймер сна`, the second row of the frozen four and the only
         one whose feature exists. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_row_height"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
        android:clickable="true"
        android:focusable="true"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/overflow_row_pad_start"
        android:paddingEnd="@dimen/overflow_row_pad_end">

        <ImageView
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_size"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_size"
            android:contentDescription="@null"
            android:scaleType="center"
            android:src="@drawable/ic_sleep_timer_clock" />

        <!--
          Label 16 after the 24 icon box - card-x 56 in the compact row. Its width
          is what is left after the trailing value's 70, and the value is GONE
          rather than INVISIBLE when the timer is off, so the label then takes the
          row's full remaining width.
        -->
        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer_label"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/overflow_label_gap"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:text="@string/sleep_timer_title"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Medium.15_22"
            android:textColor="@color/text_primary" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer_trailing"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_trailing_width"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Regular.14_20"
            android:textColor="@color/primary"
            android:visibility="gone"
            tools:text="24 мин"
            tools:visibility="visible" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!--
      `Menu row / Сообщить о проблеме` 2517:2104, the third of the frozen four and
      the second whose feature exists (G3).

      52 pitch, so the 4dp gap sits between the two 48dp rows and neither of them
      carries a margin of its own. The glyph is `Icon / alert` in the menu's
      `textSecondary` rather than in `error`: it names an action, it is not a
      warning about one.

      No trailing value. Only Таймер сна has one in the frozen menu, and only when
      a timer is armed.
    -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/player_overflow_report_problem"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_row_height"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/player_overflow_row_gap"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
        android:clickable="true"
        android:focusable="true"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/overflow_row_pad_start"
        android:paddingEnd="@dimen/overflow_row_pad_end">

        <ImageView
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_size"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_size"
            android:contentDescription="@null"
            android:scaleType="center"
            android:src="@drawable/ic_player_overflow_alert" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_report_problem_label"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/overflow_label_gap"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:text="@string/report_title"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Medium.15_22"
            android:textColor="@color/text_primary" />
    </LinearLayout>
</LinearLayout>
